{"chunk_id": "6b07ca2f69b6", "text": "On the sixth night after Rama\u2019s exile, King Dasharatha awakens tormented by grief and realizes his suffering is the fruit of a past sin. Speaking to Queen Kaushalya, he reflects on karma: one who acts without considering consequences must eventually reap the result. In his youth he prided himself on the skill of shooting by sound alone. While hunting on the banks of the Sarayu during the rainy season, he heard what he believed was an elephant filling itself with water and loosed a poisoned arrow. Instead he struck a young ascetic boy who had come to draw water for his blind, aged parents. The dying youth laments not his own death but the fate of his helpless parents. Dasharatha\u2019s recollection reveals the moral cause of his present anguish and foreshadows the curse and tragic destiny tied to Rama\u2019s exile.\nKing Dasharatha confesses that his present misery comes from a youthful mistake when he accidentally killed a hermit boy by shooting at a sound.\nThemes: karma and consequences, tragic mistake, confession and guilt, filial devotion, fate and suffering", "vector": [0.015457387082278728, -0.01361408643424511, -0.00775502622127533, -0.02154027670621872, -0.01244885753840208, 0.009440328925848007, -0.019907640293240547, -0.015812881290912628, -0.026912178844213486, -0.0015141392359510064, 0.02418672852218151, -0.0011076257796958089, -0.0071230377070605755, 0.019354648888111115, -0.009578576311469078, 0.0016581470845267177, 0.054825007915496826, -0.02269892208278179, 0.040289271622896194, -0.0231334138661623, 0.012047281488776207, -0.009249416179955006, -0.010059150867164135, -0.004522668197751045, -0.01826183684170246, -0.002562516136094928, 0.011270462535321712, -0.02418672852218151, 0.018011674284934998, -0.03444337472319603, -0.012494940310716629, -0.013350758701562881, 0.0027583667542785406, -0.01809067279100418, -0.03699766471982002, 0.028228823095560074, -0.007932772859930992, -0.006056556943804026, -0.00056204